### `loss.py`

```
estimate_loss(data, model, eval_iters=100)      [line 5]
  @torch.no_grad()
  Averages cross-entropy over eval_iters batches per split
  → {'train': float, 'val': float}
```

### `metrics.py`

```
Metrics(number_of_steps=5, mask_ratio=0.15)     [line 5]
  .__call__(data, model, tokenizer)             [line 59]
    @torch.no_grad(); runs .step() number_of_steps times, averages
    → {'perplexity', 'rouge1', 'rougeL', 'bertscore', 'masked_accuracy'}
  .step(data, model, tokenizer)                 [line 14]
    1. Perplexity  — exp(cross_entropy) on val batch
    2. ROUGE-1/L   — generate gen_len tokens from prompt half, compare to reference half
    3. BERTScore   — same generated vs reference, semantic F1
    4. Masked acc  — argmax prediction vs target at 15% random positions
```

